*.sw?

# KEEP LAST. The WASM core is VENDORED, not fetched at runtime: the real build output has
# to ship inside the commit, because the CDN fallback that used to cover it was deliberately
# removed (see src/lib/heart.ts). Those bytes look exactly like a build artifact, so they
# are precisely what a future `*.wasm` / `dist`-style / `public/assets/**` rule would sweep
# up by accident — and the failure is silent, not loud: the deploy 404s the glue script,
# loadCore() degrades to the JS fallback, and no user ever sees an error. Git resolves a
# path by the LAST pattern that matches it, so these negations only protect anything while
# they stay at the bottom of the file. Add new ignore rules ABOVE this block. (No-ops as
# written today, by design.)
#
# BOTH paths, and the order below is the order of importance. groloo-core/<build>/ is the
# LIVE core the app imports — it is the one whose loss is an outage-shaped nothing. heart/
# is the previous core, kept on disk as the rollback: it earns its negation only for as long
# as rolling back is a thing anyone might need to do, and it should be deleted (folder and
# line together) once the successor has shipped and settled. Whichever folder is live must
# be listed here; the guard in .github/workflows/ci.yml derives that name from
# src/lib/heart.ts, so if this list ever falls behind a rename, CI says so out loud.
!public/assets/groloo-core/
!public/assets/heart/

# ffmpeg.wasm core — 32 MB, copied from node_modules by scripts/copy-ffmpeg.mjs
public/ffmpeg/
